      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "You might add drone fly system toggle for it.\nToggle 1: Flying horizonally. To go down, simply pull joystick down. Camera go up/down is using grip button. This is \"horizontal\" fly mode, so it stays at same height where you go. Can used for overview videos and simple photography where horizontal is important. This mode is now in VRChat.\nToggle 2: Here the joystick for up/down and camera panning up/down swapped. Now you will fly in the direction of camera look direction. Means if you pull joystick left/right/up/down drone will rotate and will rotate down as will. Not more horizontal, means if you fly forward and drone is looking down, it will fly down in the looking direction. Useful for world exploring filming. Still horizontal because camera is not tilting, but it's same as walking around and where camera must stay horizontal.\nToggle 3: Same as toggle 2, now with camera tilting. Here it will not stay horizontal, more for experienced drone flying, can even go upside down. Because left-right is now as tilting, so if you want go left for example, you tilt it first 90 degree, then pull up to make turn possible. This is sort of rollercoaster filming due tilting.\nIdea if you switch to Toggle 1, drone can restored automatic to horizontal level. In Toggle 2, it can stays tilted, but control is swapped.\nBUT!\nDownside: you're disturbing some creators on Booth.pm. There is Virtual Drone asset, and we have VRCLens too which has drone feature too. With adding more features, you're blocking the creator sales a bit. As developer in respecting existing other works, we should not add too much features on it, players must accept it, and if they want more, PAY for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
